TITLE:: RLNetworkPage
summary:: Networks shown on HomewareVisuals' network page: side by side, nodes holding an object and arrows with their labels
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLNetwork, Classes/RLAutomorphism, Classes/RCVisuals, Classes/RLChordGraph, Classes/RLLattice, Classes/RLCanonPage, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
The network page of HomewareVisuals (code::/network/::) draws transformational networks side by side, each in a frame: nodes holding an object, arrows with their labels. A network moved again and again by an automorphism (link::Classes/RLNetwork#-iterate::) is a row of frames: the same arrows, other chords in the nodes; where the automorphism changes the labels, one sees that too. The page only draws. Messages go through link::Classes/RCVisuals::.

code::
~cd = RLRelationContext.cubeDance;  ~sp = ~cd.space;
~cell = RLNetwork.chain(~cd, [~sp.major(2), ~sp.chord(2, \aug), ~sp.minor(7)], [\U, \U]);
~cells = ~cell.iterate(RLAutomorphism.transposition(~cd, 5), 11);          // "Take a Bow": a fourth up, 12 cells
RLNetworkPage.show(~cells, "Take a Bow", captions: ~cells.collect { |c, k| "cell " ++ (k + 1) });
RLNetworkPage.at(3);                                                        // the frame that plays
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: show
argument:: networks
One link::Classes/RLNetwork:: or a list of them, one frame each.
argument:: title
argument:: places
One code::[x, y]:: for each node, between -1 and 1, y downwards, the same in every frame; round a circle when nil (link::#*places::).
argument:: captions
One text for each frame.

METHOD:: at
The frame that plays; nil for none.

METHOD:: places
The places of n nodes round a circle, the first at the top (three make a triangle).
